TAXING DISTRICTS.\
SENATE BILL 1108 SIMPLY SETS REASONABLE LIMITS ON THE PROPERTY\
TAX PORTION OF BUDGET GROWTH SO PROPERTY TAXES WILL NOT CONTINUE\
TO BALLOON AND CITIZENS ARE NOT TAXED OUT OF THEIR HOMES.\
SETTING REASONABLE LIMITS ON PROPERTY TAX BUDGET GROWTH IS NOT\
GOING TO HAMSTRING THE ABILITY TO PROVIDE NECESSARY SERVICES.\
IT MAY, HOWEVER, REQUIRE SOME PRIORITIZATION AND TO RETHINK\
SERVICES THAT MAY NOT BE NECESSARY OR THE LEVEL OF SERVICES\
PROVIDED.\
IN MANY CASES, THE LEVEL OF SERVICES IS FAR HIGHER THAN THE\
CITIZENS WANT OR NEED.\
NOW, I LIVE IN THE CITY OF NAPA.\
IN MY EXPERIENCE, THERE ARE FAR MORE TAXPAYERS ASKING FOR LIMITS\
ON TAXATION THAN THERE ARE TAXPAYERS REQUESTING MORE OR BETTER\
SERVICES.\
WE NEED TO GET BACK TO OUR FOUNDING PRINCIPLES.\
NAMELY, THAT GOVERNMENT IS TO SERVE THE PEOPLE, NOT THE PEOPLE\
SERVED THE GOVERNMENT.\
TAXPAYERS WANT MORE SAY IN THE LEVEL OF TAXES THEY ARE REQUIRED\
TO PAY, NOT LESS.\
THEY WANT BETTER AND STRONGER SIDEBOARDS ON WHAT LOCAL\
GOVERNMENTS CAN SPEND, NOT LESS.\
IF THERE IS A LEGITIMATE NEED, TAXPAYERS CAN STILL VOTE TO\
OVERRIDE THE LIMITATION THAT'S PROVIDED IN SENATE BILL 1108.\
IN CLOSING, MR. CHAIRMAN, I FIND IT AUDIT THAT WHEN IT IS THE\
